abstract: >-
  Trains and evaluates a BiLSTM + Bahdanau-attention model that forecasts a
  vehicle's serving cell 1-7 seconds ahead from the FUMD-AI preprocessing
  workflow's AI-ready labeled dataset, then postprocesses the results:
  training-metrics comparison across runs and spatial mapping of
  handover/migration events. Six Jupyter notebooks cover the pipeline
  from windowed dataset to mapped migration events, including an optional
  alternate entry point that combines several runs into one larger
  training set, plus a local/interactive orchestrator notebook
  (run_pipeline.ipynb) and Slurm/Singularity submission templates for the
  GPU training/evaluation steps.
